  "note": "Re-judged 2026-11-03 by an independent auditor who authored none of 6b105ebc58, c782411791 or 29f15481fa. RFC 2545 Section 3 read: \"The link-local address shall be included in the Next Hop field if and only if the BGP speaker shares a common subnet with the entity identified by the global IPv6 address carried in the Network Address of Next Hop field and the peer the route is being advertised to.\" Moved units since the last stamp: TestRFC2545ForwardPolicyOwnGlobalJointSubnet (6b105ebc58) lost only its operation subcases, which drove an MP_REACH set operation through the in-process egress step that commit deleted, so no producer remains for them; the raw subcases on both rails (rs dispatched through rs-export) keep every assertion: exactly one IPv6 policy call, two sections, the native field exactly own global plus own link-local on the common link and own global alone off it, the legacy sibling's NLRI and NEXT_HOP unchanged, and they now run the production step order (buildOrderedEgressSteps) instead of a hand-built one. checkRFC2545NextHops (c782411791) changed only linkLocalAt to labconfig.LinkLocalAt, the same arithmetic. 29f15481fa adds hand-written break records on checkRFC2545NextHops that answer question 2 for the interop carrier: positive citation 4, link_scope.go:226 speaker case returning no link-local while Ze's own global and FRR share the /64, red at assertion 4 with 1-3 green; negative citation 6, the pair link_scope.go:119 (joint condition reduced to the peer half) and :239 (third party takes the configured link-local), together the leaf-decides-alone defect the negative tag names, red at assertion 6, each alone green because the off-link global is also a third party the neighbor table cannot pair. The two guards enforce distinct obligations (the joint subnet condition, and that the second address is the next hop's own), so the pair shows no redundant guard. Producers linkLocalNextHop and thirdPartyLinkLocal are unchanged since the last stamp, so the gap stands. Verdict: partial. Tested: \"only if the BGP speaker shares a common subnet with the entity identified by the global IPv6 address carried in the Network Address of Next Hop field and the peer the route is being advertised to.\" Gap: \"The link-local address shall be included in the Next Hop field if\". Producer: internal/component/bgp/reactor/link_scope.go::thirdPartyLinkLocal, with linkLocalNextHop. Earlier judgements are in this file's git history.",
